window.DD_TESTS = [{"exam":"sat","set":1,"title":{"en":"SAT Reading and Writing — Practice module 1","th":"SAT Reading and Writing — ชุดฝึก 1"},"note":{"en":"One 27-question module in Digital SAT format. DeepDistrict practice — not an official College Board test.","th":"1 โมดูล 27 ข้อ รูปแบบ Digital SAT — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการของ College Board"},"minutes":32,"kinds":{"sat":27},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Nang yai, a form of Thai shadow theatre, uses large panels of carved leather that performers hold above their heads while they dance in front of a lit screen. Because a single panel can weigh several kilograms and a performance may last for hours, the dancers must be physically ______.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["ornate","fragile","hesitant","robust"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The dancers carry heavy panels for hours, so they must be strong and able to endure: 'robust'. 'Fragile' is the opposite, 'hesitant' describes uncertainty rather than physical strength, and 'ornate' describes decoration, not a person's body.","th":"นักแสดงต้องถือแผ่นหนังหนักหลายกิโลกรัมเป็นเวลาหลายชั่วโมง จึงต้องแข็งแรงทนทาน คือ robust ส่วน fragile (เปราะบาง) มีความหมายตรงข้าม hesitant (ลังเล) ไม่เกี่ยวกับร่างกาย และ ornate (ประดับประดา) ใช้กับสิ่งของ ไม่ใช่ความแข็งแรงของคน"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"m","passage":"The following text is from a short story.\nPim had not visited her grandmother's house in Lampang for eleven years. The mango tree still leaned over the well, and the narrow path still curved past the spirit house. What struck Pim most, though, was the quiet: no traffic, no voices, only the slow creak of the wooden shutters in the wind.","stem":"As used in the text, what does the word \"struck\" most nearly mean?","choices":["cancelled","impressed","hit","defeated"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The quiet is something Pim notices strongly, so 'struck' means 'impressed' (made a strong impression on her). 'Hit' is the physical meaning, 'defeated' is the sense used in contests, and 'cancelled' is the sense of 'struck from a list'; none fits a feeling caused by silence.","th":"ความเงียบเป็นสิ่งที่ทำให้พิมรู้สึกสะดุดใจมากที่สุด struck ในที่นี้จึงหมายถึง impressed (สร้างความประทับใจ/สะดุดใจ) ส่วน hit (ตี) เป็นความหมายทางกายภาพ defeated (เอาชนะ) และ cancelled (ขีดฆ่าออก) เป็นความหมายอื่นของคำนี้ที่ไม่เข้ากับบริบท"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-quantitative","difficulty":"e","passage":"A student tested whether soaking rice seeds in water before planting affects how many of them sprout. She soaked four groups of 100 seeds for different lengths of time and counted the seeds that had germinated after one week. She concluded that soaking helps, but that a longer soak does not always lead to more germination, since ______","table":{"title":"Rice seeds germinated after one week (out of 100)","rows":[["Soaking time (hours)","Seeds germinated"],["0","54"],["12","71"],["24","88"],["48","83"]]},"stem":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?","choices":["the group soaked for 12 hours had more germinated seeds than the group soaked for 24 hours.","the group that was not soaked had the fewest germinated seeds of the four groups.","the group soaked for 48 hours had fewer germinated seeds than the group soaked for 24 hours.","every group had more than 80 germinated seeds after one week."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"To show that a longer soak is not always better, the student needs a case where more soaking gave fewer sprouts: 48 hours gave 83, fewer than the 88 at 24 hours. The unsoaked group having the fewest is true but shows only that soaking helps. The 12-hour group (71) did not beat the 24-hour group, and not every group had more than 80 (54 and 71).","th":"ต้องหากรณีที่แช่นานขึ้นแต่งอกน้อยลง คือแช่ 48 ชั่วโมงงอก 83 เมล็ด น้อยกว่าแช่ 24 ชั่วโมงที่งอก 88 เมล็ด การที่กลุ่มไม่แช่งอกน้อยที่สุดเป็นจริงแต่แสดงเพียงว่าการแช่ช่วยได้ กลุ่ม 12 ชั่วโมง (71) ไม่ได้มากกว่ากลุ่ม 24 ชั่วโมง และไม่ใช่ทุกกลุ่มที่งอกเกิน 80 เมล็ด (54 และ 71)"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"An economist studying street-food vendors in Bangkok found that vendors who accept QR-code payments report higher daily sales than vendors who accept only cash. However, the vendors who accept QR codes were also much more likely to be located near office buildings, where customers tend to spend more per meal even when they pay in cash. Therefore, the higher sales reported by vendors who accept QR codes ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["indicate that vendors near office buildings rarely accept cash payments.","may be explained at least partly by where those vendors are located rather than by the payment method itself.","show that office workers prefer to pay for street food in cash.","prove that offering QR-code payments causes customers to spend more on each meal."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The text points out a second difference between the groups: location. Since customers near offices spend more even in cash, location could account for some of the higher sales. 'Prove that QR payments cause' ignores this problem; the text never says office workers prefer cash; and it says nothing about vendors near offices refusing cash.","th":"ข้อความชี้ว่าผู้ค้าที่รับ QR มักอยู่ใกล้อาคารสำนักงานซึ่งลูกค้าจ่ายมากกว่าแม้จ่ายเงินสด ยอดขายที่สูงกว่าจึงอาจเกิดจากทำเลมากกว่าวิธีชำระเงิน การบอกว่า 'พิสูจน์ว่า QR ทำให้ลูกค้าจ่ายมากขึ้น' ละเลยปัญหานี้ ข้อความไม่ได้บอกว่าพนักงานออฟฟิศชอบเงินสด และไม่ได้บอกว่าผู้ค้าใกล้สำนักงานไม่รับเงินสด"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"m","passage":"Poison dart frogs of Central and South America are among the most brightly coloured animals on Earth. The vivid colours of the frog's skin ______ predators that the animal is toxic and should not be eaten.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["has warned","warns","warn","is warning"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The subject of the verb is 'colours' (plural), not 'skin' or 'frog', so the plural verb 'warn' is needed. 'Warns', 'has warned' and 'is warning' are all singular forms that would agree only with a singular subject.","th":"ประธานของกริยาคือ colours (พหูพจน์) ไม่ใช่ skin หรือ frog จึงต้องใช้ warn ส่วน warns, has warned และ is warning เป็นรูปเอกพจน์ ใช้กับประธานเอกพจน์เท่านั้น"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"rhetorical-synthesis","difficulty":"e","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- The Thai alphabet has 44 consonant letters.\n- It developed from the Old Khmer script.\n- Tradition holds that it was created in 1283 under King Ramkhamhaeng of Sukhothai.\n- Thai is written from left to right.\n- Spaces in written Thai usually mark the ends of phrases or sentences, not the gaps between words.","stem":"The student wants to describe the origins of the Thai alphabet. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Thai alphabet developed from the Old Khmer script, and tradition holds that it was created in 1283 under King Ramkhamhaeng.","The Thai alphabet, which has 44 consonant letters, is written from left to right.","In written Thai, spaces usually mark the ends of phrases or sentences.","Thai is written from left to right, and spaces do not usually appear between words."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Only the sentence about the Old Khmer script and the traditional date of 1283 explains where the alphabet came from. The other sentences describe how Thai looks or is written today (number of letters, direction, spacing), not its origins.","th":"มีเพียงประโยคที่กล่าวถึงอักษรขอมโบราณและปี 1283 สมัยพ่อขุนรามคำแหงที่อธิบายที่มาของอักษรไทย ประโยคอื่นบอกลักษณะการเขียนในปัจจุบัน (จำนวนพยัญชนะ ทิศทางการเขียน การเว้นวรรค) ไม่ใช่ที่มา"}}]}},{"exam":"sat","set":2,"title":{"en":"SAT Reading and Writing — Practice module 2","th":"SAT Reading and Writing — ชุดฝึก 2"},"note":{"en":"One 27-question module in Digital SAT format. DeepDistrict practice — not an official College Board test.","th":"1 โมดูล 27 ข้อ รูปแบบ Digital SAT — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการของ College Board"},"minutes":32,"kinds":{"sat":27},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Before recording technology existed, a folk song survived only if people remembered it and taught it to others. Many songs from rural Isan were ______ in exactly this way, passed from parents to children over many generations until researchers finally wrote them down in the twentieth century.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["preserved","exaggerated","invented","forbidden"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The songs 'survived' because people remembered them and taught them, so they were 'preserved' (kept in existence). 'Invented' would describe how a song begins, not how it survives; 'forbidden' and 'exaggerated' do not fit songs being passed on faithfully.","th":"เพลงอยู่รอดมาได้เพราะคนจดจำและสอนต่อกัน จึงหมายถึง preserved (รักษาไว้) ส่วน invented (คิดค้นขึ้น) พูดถึงการเริ่มต้นของเพลง ไม่ใช่การอยู่รอด forbidden (ถูกห้าม) และ exaggerated (ถูกพูดเกินจริง) ไม่เข้ากับการสืบทอดเพลง"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"m","passage":"The following text is from a short story.\nFor thirty years, Mrs. Chantra had opened her noodle stall at five in the morning. When a café with glass walls and a menu in three languages opened across the street, her neighbours warned that she would lose her customers. Mrs. Chantra watched the young people lining up for iced coffee. Then she wiped her counter, lit her stove, and set out her plastic stools exactly as she always had.","stem":"Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To portray a character's steady commitment to her routine despite changes around her","To show a character deciding to change the way she runs her business","To explain why the new café is more popular than the noodle stall","To describe the history of street food in a Thai neighbourhood"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The new café and the neighbours' warning represent change, and Mrs. Chantra responds by doing everything 'exactly as she always had'. The text does not explain the café's popularity, does not give a history of street food, and shows her keeping, not changing, her routine.","th":"ร้านกาแฟใหม่และคำเตือนของเพื่อนบ้านแสดงถึงความเปลี่ยนแปลง แต่นางจันทราก็ยังทำทุกอย่างเหมือนเดิม จึงเป็นการแสดงความมั่นคงต่อกิจวัตรของตัวละคร ข้อความไม่ได้อธิบายว่าทำไมร้านกาแฟได้รับความนิยม ไม่ได้เล่าประวัติอาหารริมทาง และตัวละครไม่ได้ตัดสินใจเปลี่ยนวิธีทำธุรกิจ"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"central-ideas","difficulty":"m","passage":"A gecko can run up a glass window without using glue or suction. Each of its toes is covered with millions of tiny hairs, and each hair splits into hundreds of even tinier tips. These tips come so close to a surface that weak attractions between molecules hold them in place. No single tip holds much weight, but together they produce more than enough force to support the gecko's entire body.","stem":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["A single hair on a gecko's toe is strong enough to hold up the whole animal.","Geckos cling to surfaces through the combined effect of many tiny forces produced by the hairs on their toes.","Geckos are unable to climb surfaces that are as smooth as glass.","Geckos produce a sticky substance that allows them to climb smooth walls."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The text explains that weak forces at millions of tips add up to enough force to hold the gecko. It directly rules out glue, says that no single tip holds much weight, and begins by saying geckos can climb glass.","th":"ข้อความอธิบายว่าแรงดึงดูดเล็ก ๆ จากปลายขนจำนวนมหาศาลรวมกันจนพอจะยึดตัวตุ๊กแกไว้ได้ ข้อความบอกชัดว่าไม่ได้ใช้กาว บอกว่าปลายขนแต่ละเส้นรับน้ำหนักได้น้อย และเริ่มต้นด้วยการบอกว่าตุ๊กแกปีนกระจกได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"Astronomers observing a distant star noticed that its brightness dips by the same small amount every 12 days. Regular dips like these are often caused by a planet passing in front of a star. A dark spot on the star's surface, rotating in and out of view, can also cause regular dips, but such spots usually grow and shrink over a few weeks, which makes the dips vary in depth. Because the dips have stayed exactly the same depth throughout two years of observation, the astronomers concluded that ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["the star has no dark spots anywhere on its surface.","a passing planet is a more likely cause of the dips than a rotating spot.","a planet could not produce dips that stay the same depth.","the star must rotate exactly once every 12 days."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Spots would make the dips change in depth; the dips have not changed, so a planet is the better explanation. The evidence does not show that the star has no spots at all, only that spots are unlikely to cause these dips. A 12-day rotation would matter only for the spot explanation, which the evidence weakens, and the text implies that a planet can produce dips of constant depth.","th":"จุดมืดบนดาวทำให้ความลึกของการหรี่แสงเปลี่ยนไป แต่ความลึกคงที่ตลอดสองปี จึงสรุปว่าดาวเคราะห์โคจรผ่านน่าจะเป็นสาเหตุมากกว่า หลักฐานไม่ได้แสดงว่าดาวไม่มีจุดมืดเลย การหมุนรอบตัวทุก 12 วันเกี่ยวกับคำอธิบายแบบจุดมืดซึ่งถูกหักล้าง และข้อความบอกเป็นนัยว่าดาวเคราะห์ทำให้หรี่แสงคงที่ได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"m","passage":"When archaeologists first reached the limestone cave in 2015, they found blackened ceilings and layers of ash on the floor. Local villagers explained that by then, their families ______ the cave as a shelter during storms for centuries.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["had used","will have used","use","are using"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The using of the cave happened over a long period before another past moment ('by then', 2015), so the past perfect 'had used' is correct. 'Use' and 'are using' are present forms, and 'will have used' refers to the future, none of which fits a period ending in 2015.","th":"การใช้ถ้ำเกิดขึ้นต่อเนื่องก่อนจุดเวลาในอดีต (by then คือปี 2015) จึงใช้ past perfect คือ had used ส่วน use และ are using เป็นปัจจุบัน และ will have used เป็นอนาคต ไม่เข้ากับช่วงเวลาที่จบในปี 2015"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"m","passage":"To make traditional sa paper, workers first soak and boil strips of mulberry bark until they are soft. They then beat the bark into a pulp and spread it evenly across a screen floating in a tank of water. ______ they lift the screen out of the water and leave it in the sun until the sheet of paper is dry.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In contrast,","Finally,","For instance,","Previously,"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The text describes steps in order ('first', 'then'), and drying the sheet is the last step, so 'Finally' fits. 'Previously' would place this step before the others, 'In contrast' signals an opposing idea, and 'For instance' introduces an example rather than the next step.","th":"ข้อความเรียงขั้นตอนตามลำดับ (first, then) และการตากแผ่นกระดาษเป็นขั้นตอนสุดท้าย จึงใช้ Finally ส่วน Previously ทำให้ขั้นตอนนี้อยู่ก่อนขั้นอื่น In contrast แสดงความขัดแย้ง และ For instance ใช้ยกตัวอย่าง"}}]}},{"exam":"sat","set":3,"title":{"en":"SAT Reading and Writing — Practice module 3","th":"SAT Reading and Writing — ชุดฝึก 3"},"note":{"en":"One 27-question module in Digital SAT format. DeepDistrict practice — not an official College Board test.","th":"1 โมดูล 27 ข้อ รูปแบบ Digital SAT — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการของ College Board"},"minutes":32,"kinds":{"sat":27},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Muay Thai is often called \"the art of eight limbs\" because, unlike boxers, who strike only with their fists, muay Thai fighters ______ their fists, elbows, knees, and shins to strike an opponent.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["decorate","neglect","employ","conceal"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The 'eight limbs' are the body parts fighters use to strike, so they 'employ' (use) them. 'Conceal' (hide) and 'neglect' (fail to use) contradict the idea of striking with them, and 'decorate' has nothing to do with fighting.","th":"'แปดอวัยวะ' คือส่วนของร่างกายที่นักมวยใช้ในการโจมตี จึงใช้ employ (ใช้) ส่วน conceal (ซ่อน) และ neglect (ละเลย) ขัดกับการใช้โจมตี และ decorate (ตกแต่ง) ไม่เกี่ยวกับการต่อสู้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"h","passage":"Economist Arthit Wongsa's new model of informal labour markets does not ______ earlier theories so much as refine them: it keeps their central assumptions about how workers move between jobs while correcting the way those theories treated seasonal farm work.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["overturn","resemble","inform","extend"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The structure 'does not X so much as refine' requires X to contrast with refining, and the colon says the model 'keeps their central assumptions'. 'Overturn' (reject entirely) is the opposite of keeping assumptions. 'Extend' is close in meaning to 'refine', so there would be no contrast; 'resemble' and 'inform' do not describe what a new model does to older theories in a way that contrasts with refining.","th":"โครงสร้าง does not X so much as refine ต้องการคำที่ตรงข้ามกับการปรับปรุง และข้อความบอกว่าแบบจำลองยังคงสมมติฐานหลักไว้ จึงเป็น overturn (ล้มล้าง) ส่วน extend (ขยาย) มีความหมายใกล้กับ refine จึงไม่เกิดความขัดแย้ง resemble (คล้าย) และ inform (ให้ข้อมูล) ไม่ได้ตรงข้ามกับการปรับปรุง"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-textual","difficulty":"m","passage":"Males of a small frog species found in Southeast Asian forests often call from inside hollow bamboo stems. Researchers hypothesize that the frogs choose these sites because the hollow stems amplify their calls, allowing the calls to reach females that are farther away.","stem":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the researchers' hypothesis?","choices":["Calls of frogs inside bamboo stems were measurably louder at a distance of ten metres than calls of similar-sized frogs calling from open leaves.","Males calling from bamboo stems were, on average, larger than males calling from open leaves.","Females of the species often lay their eggs in rainwater that collects inside bamboo stems.","Males of the species call most often on rainy nights, whether from bamboo stems or from leaves."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The hypothesis is that bamboo stems make calls louder at a distance. Calls from stems being louder at ten metres than calls of similar-sized frogs on leaves shows this while ruling out size as the cause. Egg-laying suggests a different reason for using bamboo, larger males could explain louder calls without any amplification, and calling on rainy nights says nothing about volume.","th":"สมมติฐานคือกระบอกไผ่ช่วยขยายเสียงให้ดังไปได้ไกล ผลที่ว่าเสียงจากในกระบอกไผ่ดังกว่าที่ระยะ 10 เมตร เมื่อเทียบกับกบขนาดเท่ากันบนใบไม้ สนับสนุนโดยตรงและตัดเรื่องขนาดตัวออก การวางไข่ในน้ำในกระบอกไผ่เป็นเหตุผลอื่น กบตัวผู้ที่ใหญ่กว่าอาจทำให้เสียงดังโดยไม่เกี่ยวกับไผ่ และการร้องในคืนฝนตกไม่เกี่ยวกับความดังของเสียง"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"A psychologist found that students who studied a list of vocabulary words in the evening and were tested after a night's sleep recalled more words than students who studied in the morning and were tested that evening, the same number of hours later. Some critics suggested that the morning group simply encountered more distracting information during the day. To test this, the psychologist added a third group that studied in the morning and then rested quietly, awake, in a dim room until the test. If this group's recall turns out to be similar to that of the original morning group, it would suggest that ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["studying in the morning generally leads to better recall than studying in the evening.","resting quietly while awake helps memory just as much as sleeping does.","daytime distractions were the main reason the morning group recalled fewer words.","sleep itself, rather than simply avoiding daytime distractions, helped the evening group remember more words."],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The quiet-rest group avoids distractions but does not sleep. If it does no better than the morning group, avoiding distractions did not help, so sleep is the likelier reason for the evening group's advantage. That result would count against distractions as the main cause and against quiet rest being as good as sleep, and the original finding showed the evening group, not the morning group, recalling more.","th":"กลุ่มที่พักเงียบ ๆ ไม่เจอสิ่งรบกวนแต่ไม่ได้นอน ถ้าจำได้ไม่ต่างจากกลุ่มเช้า แสดงว่าการเลี่ยงสิ่งรบกวนไม่ได้ช่วย การนอนหลับจึงน่าจะเป็นเหตุที่กลุ่มเย็นจำได้มากกว่า ผลนี้ขัดกับการบอกว่าสิ่งรบกวนเป็นสาเหตุหลัก ขัดกับการบอกว่าการพักผ่อนช่วยได้เท่าการนอน และผลเดิมแสดงว่ากลุ่มเย็นจำได้มากกว่ากลุ่มเช้า"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"h","passage":"After the severe floods of 2011, engineers who studied Bangkok's drainage system reached a sobering ______ the city's canals, many of them narrowed by decades of construction along their banks, could carry only a fraction of the water they had once handled.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["conclusion, which","conclusion, that","conclusion,","conclusion:"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The first part is a complete clause, and what follows states the conclusion itself, so a colon is correct. A comma would create a comma splice between two independent clauses, a comma before 'that' wrongly separates the noun 'conclusion' from the clause that tells what the conclusion was, and 'which' makes the sentence ungrammatical because the clause after it already has its own subject, 'the city's canals'.","th":"ส่วนแรกเป็นประโยคสมบูรณ์ และส่วนหลังบอกเนื้อหาของข้อสรุป จึงใช้ : การใช้จุลภาคเป็น comma splice การใส่จุลภาคหน้า that แยกคำนาม conclusion ออกจากอนุประโยคที่บอกเนื้อหาของข้อสรุปโดยไม่ถูกต้อง และการใช้ which ทำให้ผิดไวยากรณ์เพราะอนุประโยคหลังมีประธานของตัวเองแล้ว (the city's canals)"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"m","passage":"Most spiders build webs and wait for insects to fly into them. Jumping spiders, ______ build no webs for hunting; they stalk their prey and then leap onto it from a distance of many times their own body length.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["by contrast,","for example,","therefore,","similarly,"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Jumping spiders behave differently from 'most spiders': they hunt without webs. 'By contrast' signals this difference. 'For example' would present jumping spiders as an example of web-building, 'therefore' implies a cause-and-effect link, and 'similarly' suggests they behave like other spiders.","th":"แมงมุมกระโดดมีพฤติกรรมต่างจากแมงมุมส่วนใหญ่ คือล่าเหยื่อโดยไม่ใช้ใย จึงใช้ by contrast ส่วน for example ทำให้ดูเหมือนเป็นตัวอย่างของแมงมุมที่ชักใย therefore แสดงเหตุและผล และ similarly แสดงความเหมือน"}}]}},{"exam":"ielts","set":1,"title":{"en":"IELTS Academic — Practice test 1 (Reading + Writing)","th":"IELTS Academic — ชุดฝึก 1 (Reading + Writing)"},"note":{"en":"Reading: 3 passages, 40 questions, 60 minutes. Writing: Task 1 + Task 2, 60 minutes. DeepDistrict practice — not an official IELTS test.","th":"Reading 3 บทความ 40 ข้อ 60 นาที · Writing Task 1 + Task 2 60 นาที — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการ"},"minutes":60,"kinds":{"ielts-r":3,"ielts-w":2},"sample":{"reading":{"kind":"ielts-r","title":"Gardens above the street","difficulty":1,"paragraphs":["Look down on almost any large city from a tall building and you will see a landscape of grey and black: flat roofs covered in tar, gravel or metal, broken only by water tanks and air-conditioning units. For decades these surfaces were treated as wasted space, visited only when something needed repairing. In recent years, however, architects, local governments and ordinary residents have begun to look at them differently. Across Asia, Europe and the Americas, roofs are being covered with soil and plants, and some of them now produce vegetables, herbs and even eggs. The idea itself is not entirely new. In many hot countries, families have long kept pots of herbs and climbing plants on flat roofs. What has changed is the scale of the projects and the range of reasons that people give for building them.","The most widely discussed benefit is temperature. A dark roof absorbs a great deal of sunlight, and on a clear afternoon its surface can become far hotter than the air around it. This heat passes into the rooms below, and the people inside respond by switching on fans and air-conditioners. A layer of soil and plants changes this pattern in two ways. First, the leaves shade the roof so that less sunlight reaches it directly. Second, plants release water through their leaves, and the evaporation of this water removes heat, in much the same way that sweat cools human skin. Measurements taken on planted roofs regularly show surface temperatures well below those of bare roofs nearby, and the floors immediately beneath them are usually the ones that benefit most.","A second advantage concerns rain. In a city, most rainwater falls on hard surfaces such as roads, car parks and roofs, and it runs almost immediately into drains. During heavy storms, the drains can fill faster than they can empty, and streets flood. A planted roof behaves more like a sponge. The soil absorbs part of the rain and releases it slowly over the following hours, some of it through the plants and some through the building's pipes. For cities that experience intense monsoon rains, this delay can be valuable, because it reduces the peak amount of water that the drainage system must handle at any one moment.","Turning a roof into a garden is not simply a matter of carrying up some bags of earth. Wet soil is extremely heavy, and many older buildings were never designed to support such a load. Before any work begins, an engineer must check how much weight the structure can carry safely. Designers often reduce the load by using a special lightweight growing material, such as a mixture of coconut fibre and crushed volcanic rock, instead of ordinary garden soil. Water is the other great enemy. Beneath the plants, a roof garden needs a waterproof layer to protect the building, and a root barrier to stop roots from forcing their way into cracks. If either layer fails, repairs can be expensive, because the whole garden may have to be removed to find the leak.","The conditions on a roof are also harsher than those at ground level. Wind speeds are higher, there is often no shade at all, and the shallow soil dries out quickly. As a result, the most successful rooftop farms concentrate on crops with short roots and short growing seasons, such as leafy greens, herbs and chillies. Fruit trees are rarely attempted, because they need deep soil and can be damaged by strong winds. Some projects avoid soil completely and grow plants in channels of water to which nutrients have been added, a method known as hydroponics. This system is lighter than a soil garden and uses less water, but it depends on pumps and requires more technical knowledge to run.","For many of the people involved, the social side of rooftop gardening matters as much as the practical benefits. In crowded neighbourhoods where there are few parks, a shared roof garden can become a meeting place for residents who might otherwise never speak to one another. Schools use their roofs to teach children where food comes from, and older residents, some of whom grew up on farms, are often keen to share what they know. In several cities, groups of volunteers sell their surplus vegetables to local restaurants, and the money they earn helps to pay for seeds and tools for the following season.","It would be a mistake, however, to expect roof gardens to feed whole cities. Even if every suitable roof were planted, the amount of food produced would be small compared with what a large urban population eats each day. Building and maintaining a garden also costs money, and without regular care a roof can quickly return to bare concrete. Supporters of the movement accept these limits. They argue that the true value of rooftop farms lies not in the number of vegetables they grow, but in the combination of cooler buildings, reduced flooding and stronger communities that they bring together."],"groups":[{"type":"headings","instructions":"Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B–G from the list of headings below.","options":[{"key":"i","text":"Bringing neighbours together"},{"key":"ii","text":"Keeping buildings cool"},{"key":"iii","text":"Why farmers are leaving the countryside"},{"key":"iv","text":"Slowing the flow of rainwater"},{"key":"v","text":"The technical demands of a heavy garden"},{"key":"vi","text":"Crops that can cope with difficult conditions"},{"key":"vii","text":"The rising cost of imported vegetables"},{"key":"viii","text":"Realistic expectations about food production"},{"key":"ix","text":"New laws that require green roofs"}],"questions":[{"text":"Paragraph B","answer":["ii"]},{"text":"Paragraph C","answer":["iv"]},{"text":"Paragraph D","answer":["v"]},{"text":"Paragraph E","answer":["vi"]},{"text":"Paragraph F","answer":["i"]},{"text":"Paragraph G","answer":["viii"]}]},{"type":"tfng","instructions":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","questions":[{"text":"In the past, city roofs were usually visited only when repairs were needed.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Rooftop gardens are more common in Asia than in Europe.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]},{"text":"The top floors of a building with a planted roof gain less cooling benefit than the lower floors.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Hydroponic systems need more water than gardens that use soil.","answer":["FALSE"]}]},{"type":"note-completion","instructions":"Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.","wordLimit":{"words":1,"number":false},"context":"Creating a rooftop garden\n• Before work starts: an (11) ______ checks how much weight the structure can carry\n• To reduce weight: coconut fibre mixed with crushed volcanic (12) ______\n• Below the plants: a waterproof layer and a root (13) ______","questions":[{"text":"(11) ______","answer":["engineer"]},{"text":"(12) ______","answer":["rock"]},{"text":"(13) ______","answer":["barrier"]}]}]},"writing":[{"kind":"ielts-w","task":1,"visual":"table","prompt":"The table below shows the average amount of water used per person each day for different purposes in one city in 2000, 2010 and 2020.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.","table":{"title":"Average daily household water use per person (litres)","rows":[["Purpose","2000","2010","2020"],["Showering and bathing","62","58","49"],["Toilet flushing","45","36","28"],["Laundry","30","26","22"],["Cooking and drinking","8","9","9"],["Garden and outdoor use","25","21","12"],["Other","10","12","15"],["Total","180","162","135"]]}},{"kind":"ielts-w","task":2,"essayType":"discussion","prompt":"Some people believe that the best way to reduce traffic congestion in cities is to build more and wider roads. Others think that the money would be better spent on improving public transport.\n\nDiscuss both these views and give your own opinion.\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words."}]}},{"exam":"ielts","set":2,"title":{"en":"IELTS Academic — Practice test 2 (Reading + Writing)","th":"IELTS Academic — ชุดฝึก 2 (Reading + Writing)"},"note":{"en":"Reading: 3 passages, 40 questions, 60 minutes. Writing: Task 1 + Task 2, 60 minutes. DeepDistrict practice — not an official IELTS test.","th":"Reading 3 บทความ 40 ข้อ 60 นาที · Writing Task 1 + Task 2 60 นาที — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการ"},"minutes":60,"kinds":{"ielts-r":3,"ielts-w":2},"sample":{"reading":{"kind":"ielts-r","title":"Forests at the edge of the sea","difficulty":1,"paragraphs":["Along many tropical and subtropical coastlines, where rivers meet the sea, grow forests unlike any others. Mangroves are trees and shrubs that live in salty water, rooted in soft mud that is flooded by the tide twice a day. Few other trees can survive in such conditions, and for a long time mangrove areas were regarded as useless swamps, unpleasant to visit and difficult to cross. Large areas were cleared to make way for farms, ports, housing and ponds for raising shrimp. Today, scientists and coastal communities increasingly see mangroves in a very different light, as some of the most valuable ecosystems on the planet.","The first challenge for any plant growing in seawater is salt, which damages most plants by drawing water out of their cells. Mangrove species have developed several solutions. Some prevent most of the salt from entering in the first place, filtering it out at the surface of their roots. Others allow salt to enter but get rid of it through special glands on their leaves; on a dry day, small white salt crystals can sometimes be seen on the leaf surface. A third group stores salt in older leaves, which turn yellow and eventually fall, taking the salt with them.","The second challenge lies underground. The thick mud in which mangroves grow contains very little oxygen, which roots need in order to function. Some species solve this problem by sending up narrow, pencil-like roots that stick out above the mud, sometimes in their thousands around a single tree. These roots have tiny openings through which the tree can obtain oxygen directly from the air when the tide is low. Other species produce prop roots, which arch out from the trunk like the legs of a table and help to keep the tree stable in mud that would not otherwise support it.","Mangroves also have an unusual way of producing new plants. In many species, the seed begins to grow while it is still attached to the parent tree, forming a long, pointed seedling. When it is ready, the seedling drops. If it falls at low tide, it may push straight into the mud and begin to root. If it falls into the water, it floats, and it can survive for several weeks in seawater before it reaches a suitable place to settle. This allows mangroves to spread along coastlines and to colonise new mudbanks.","For people living on the coast, one of the most important services that mangroves provide is protection. The dense mass of roots and trunks slows down waves and reduces the force with which they reach the shore. The roots also trap sediment carried by rivers and tides, so that over time the level of the land may actually rise. After severe storms, villages that lay behind wide belts of mangroves have often suffered less damage than similar villages on open coasts. Researchers stress, however, that mangroves reduce the effects of storms rather than preventing them completely, and that a very large wave can pass through even a healthy forest.","Mangroves are also nurseries for marine life. The calm, shaded water among the roots provides shelter for young fish, crabs and shrimp, which would be eaten quickly in open water. Many of these animals move out to sea as they grow, so the health of offshore fisheries often depends on the survival of mangroves along the coast. In addition, the waterlogged mud beneath the trees stores large amounts of carbon, because dead leaves and roots decay very slowly when there is little oxygen.","Recognising these benefits, many countries have begun to replant mangroves, but the results have been mixed. In some projects, millions of seedlings were planted in places where mangroves had never grown naturally, such as mudflats that are covered by the sea for too long each day, and most of them died. Experience suggests that success depends less on the number of trees planted than on choosing the right location and the right species. The most successful projects often begin by restoring the natural flow of tidal water, for example by removing old walls built for shrimp ponds, and then allowing seedlings carried by the tide to settle by themselves."],"groups":[{"type":"tfng","instructions":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","questions":[{"text":"Mangroves can grow in conditions where most other trees cannot survive.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Mangrove areas were traditionally protected because of their value to farmers.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Salt crystals can sometimes be seen on the leaves of certain mangrove species.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Mangrove seedlings die within a few hours if they fall into seawater.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Mangrove wood is widely used by coastal communities for building boats.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]},{"text":"Planting seedlings is cheaper than restoring the natural flow of tidal water.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]}]},{"type":"table-completion","instructions":"Complete the table below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.","wordLimit":{"words":1,"number":false},"context":"How mangroves survive\nFeature | Description | Function\nSalt glands | found on the (7) ______ | remove salt from the plant\nPencil-like roots | stick out above the mud | allow the tree to obtain (8) ______\nProp roots | arch out from the trunk | keep the tree (9) ______ in soft mud\nSeedlings | float in seawater | can survive for several (10) ______ before settling","questions":[{"text":"(7) ______","answer":["leaves"]},{"text":"(8) ______","answer":["oxygen"]},{"text":"(9) ______","answer":["stable"]},{"text":"(10) ______","answer":["weeks"]}]},{"type":"mcq","instructions":"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","questions":[{"text":"According to paragraph E, mangrove roots can help to raise the level of the land by","options":[{"key":"A","text":"absorbing large amounts of rainwater."},{"key":"B","text":"trapping sediment carried by rivers and tides."},{"key":"C","text":"breaking up rocks along the shore."},{"key":"D","text":"producing new soil from fallen leaves."}],"answer":["B"]},{"text":"Why are mangroves described as nurseries for marine life?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They provide food for fish that live far out at sea."},{"key":"B","text":"They keep the sea water cool during the hottest months."},{"key":"C","text":"Young sea animals can shelter safely among their roots."},{"key":"D","text":"Fishermen raise young fish there in special ponds."}],"answer":["C"]},{"text":"According to the writer, replanting projects are most likely to succeed when","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the natural movement of the tides is restored first."},{"key":"B","text":"very large numbers of seedlings are planted quickly."},{"key":"C","text":"seedlings are planted on mudflats far from the shore."},{"key":"D","text":"only one species of mangrove is used."}],"answer":["A"]}]}]},"writing":[{"kind":"ielts-w","task":1,"visual":"table","prompt":"The table below shows the number of visitors to four types of tourist attraction in one city in 2015, 2020 and 2025.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.","table":{"title":"Visitors to tourist attractions (thousands)","rows":[["Type of attraction","2015","2020","2025"],["Museums and galleries","420","180","510"],["Theme parks","650","240","720"],["Zoos and aquariums","310","150","280"],["Historic sites","280","120","390"],["All attractions","1,660","690","1,900"]]}},{"kind":"ielts-w","task":2,"essayType":"problem-solution","prompt":"In many large cities, young adults are finding it increasingly difficult to afford a home of their own.\n\nWhat problems does this cause? What measures could be taken to solve these problems?\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words."}]}},{"exam":"ielts","set":3,"title":{"en":"IELTS Academic — Practice test 3 (Reading + Writing)","th":"IELTS Academic — ชุดฝึก 3 (Reading + Writing)"},"note":{"en":"Reading: 3 passages, 40 questions, 60 minutes. Writing: Task 1 + Task 2, 60 minutes. DeepDistrict practice — not an official IELTS test.","th":"Reading 3 บทความ 40 ข้อ 60 นาที · Writing Task 1 + Task 2 60 นาที — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการ"},"minutes":60,"kinds":{"ielts-r":3,"ielts-w":2},"sample":{"reading":{"kind":"ielts-r","title":"Saving seeds for the future","difficulty":1,"paragraphs":["Over the past century, farming has changed dramatically. In many parts of the world, farmers who once grew dozens of local varieties of rice, wheat, beans or maize have switched to a small number of modern varieties that produce higher yields. This change has helped to feed a rapidly growing population, but it has had an unexpected cost. As the old varieties stopped being planted, many of them disappeared. Seed banks were created to slow this loss. Their aim is simple: to collect and store seeds from as many types of crop as possible, so that the diversity built up by farmers over thousands of years is not lost for ever.","Why should anyone care about varieties that farmers no longer want? The answer is that an old local variety may carry characteristics that modern crops lack, such as resistance to a particular disease, or the ability to survive drought or high temperatures. Plant breeders can cross these varieties with modern ones to produce new crops that combine high yields with greater resilience. A variety that seems unimportant today may become extremely valuable if the climate changes or a new pest appears, and once a variety has vanished, it cannot be brought back.","Building a collection begins in the field. Collectors travel to farms, markets and wild areas, often in remote regions, to find plants that have not yet been stored. For each sample, they record where it was found, the conditions in which it was growing and the name that local farmers use for it. Because plants of the same variety are not identical, collectors take seeds from many different plants rather than from just one, in order to capture as much variation as possible. They must also obtain permission from landowners and governments, and many collections are now made under agreements that share any future benefits with the communities that provided the seeds.","Once the seeds arrive at the bank, they are cleaned and checked for pests and disease. They are then dried carefully until they contain very little moisture, because water inside a seed allows the chemical processes of ageing to continue. The dried seeds are sealed in airtight foil packets or glass jars and placed in cold rooms, where the temperature is kept at around minus twenty degrees Celsius. Under these conditions, the seeds of many crops can remain alive for decades, and some may survive for much longer.","Not every plant can be stored in this way. The seeds of many tropical trees, along with some fruit and nut crops, are killed by drying, so they cannot simply be placed in a freezer. Seed banks deal with these species in other ways. Some are kept as living plants in field collections, where they must be watered, protected from pests and eventually replaced. Others are stored as small pieces of plant tissue frozen in liquid nitrogen, at temperatures far below those of an ordinary cold room. Both methods are considerably more expensive than storing dried seed.","Even well-stored seeds slowly lose their ability to grow, so seed banks must check their collections regularly. In a germination test, a small number of seeds from a sample are planted, and staff count how many of them begin to grow. If the proportion falls too low, the sample must be grown in a field or greenhouse to produce fresh seed, a process known as regeneration. This is slow and costly work, and for crops that are pollinated by insects or wind, great care is needed to prevent different varieties from mixing.","Seed banks themselves are not completely safe. Collections have been damaged by floods, fires, wars and failures of electricity supply. For this reason, most banks send duplicate samples to other institutions, and a few secure back-up stores have been built inside mountains in cold regions, where the seeds would stay frozen even if the power were cut. Experts emphasise, however, that seed banks are not a substitute for farmers. Crops that continue to be grown in fields keep adapting to changing conditions, while seeds in storage remain exactly as they were on the day they were collected."],"groups":[{"type":"matching-info","instructions":"Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–G.","questions":[{"text":"the temperature at which seeds are usually stored","answer":["D"]},{"text":"examples of events that could destroy a seed collection","answer":["G"]},{"text":"details of the information noted down when seeds are collected","answer":["C"]},{"text":"a reason why a variety that seems unimportant may be useful in the future","answer":["B"]}]},{"type":"sentence-completion","instructions":"Complete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.","wordLimit":{"words":2,"number":false},"questions":[{"text":"Before collecting seeds, collectors must get permission from landowners and ______.","answer":["governments"]},{"text":"Seeds that cannot survive drying may be stored as plant tissue frozen in ______.","answer":["liquid nitrogen"]},{"text":"Growing stored seeds to produce a fresh supply is called ______.","answer":["regeneration"]},{"text":"Some back-up stores have been built inside ______ in cold regions.","answer":["mountains"]}]},{"type":"tfng","instructions":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","questions":[{"text":"Many farmers now grow fewer crop varieties than farmers did in the past.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Collectors normally take seeds from a single plant of each variety.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Under the right conditions, the seeds of many crops can survive in storage for decades.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Germination tests are carried out once every year.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]},{"text":"Seeds kept in storage continue to adapt to changes in the climate.","answer":["FALSE"]}]}]},"writing":[{"kind":"ielts-w","task":1,"visual":"process","prompt":"The table below shows the stages in recycling used glass bottles at one processing plant, and the average time each stage takes.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.","table":{"title":"Recycling glass bottles: stages and average time","rows":[["Stage","What happens","Average time"],["1. Collection","Bottles collected from homes and public bins","2 days"],["2. Sorting","Separated by colour; labels and caps removed","6 hours"],["3. Crushing","Broken into small pieces","1 hour"],["4. Cleaning","Washed; paper and metal removed","2 hours"],["5. Melting","Heated with sand in a furnace at 1,500°C","12 hours"],["6. Moulding","Shaped into new bottles and cooled","30 minutes"],["7. Delivery","Sent to drinks companies for refilling","3 days"]]}},{"kind":"ielts-w","task":2,"essayType":"two-part","prompt":"In many countries, people now spend less time cooking at home and more often buy ready-made meals or eat in restaurants.\n\nWhy is this happening? Is it a positive or a negative development?\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words."}]}},{"exam":"gate","set":1,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 GATE Program — Practice set 1","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 GATE Program — ชุดฝึก 1"},"note":{"en":"40 questions: Mathematics 15, Science 15, English 5, Thai 5. DeepDistrict practice format based on the school's published subjects — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ: คณิตศาสตร์ 15 วิทยาศาสตร์ 15 ภาษาอังกฤษ 5 ภาษาไทย 5 — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ตามวิชาที่โรงเรียนประกาศ ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ห.ร.ม. ของ 84 และ 126 เท่ากับเท่าใด","choices":["252","42","14","21"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"84 = 2²×3×7 and 126 = 2×3²×7. The HCF takes the common primes with the smaller powers: 2×3×7 = 42. (252 is the LCM, not the HCF.)","th":"84 = 2²×3×7 และ 126 = 2×3²×7 ห.ร.ม. คือผลคูณของตัวประกอบเฉพาะที่ซ้ำกันโดยใช้เลขชี้กำลังน้อยกว่า = 2×3×7 = 42 (252 คือ ค.ร.น. ไม่ใช่ ห.ร.ม.)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"รถยนต์คันหนึ่งขับจากเมือง ก ไปเมือง ข ด้วยอัตราเร็ว 60 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง และขับกลับทางเดิมด้วยอัตราเร็ว 40 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง อัตราเร็วเฉลี่ยตลอดการเดินทางไป–กลับเป็นกี่กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง","choices":["48","45","52","50"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Average speed = total distance ÷ total time, not the mean of the speeds. Take the distance as 120 km: time = 2 h + 3 h = 5 h, total 240 km, so 240 ÷ 5 = 48 km/h.","th":"อัตราเร็วเฉลี่ย = ระยะทางทั้งหมด ÷ เวลาทั้งหมด ไม่ใช่ค่าเฉลี่ยของอัตราเร็ว สมมติระยะทาง 120 กม. ไปใช้ 2 ชม. กลับใช้ 3 ชม. รวม 240 กม. ใน 5 ชม. ได้ 240 ÷ 5 = 48 กม./ชม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"รูปสี่เหลี่ยมจัตุรัสยาวด้านละ 14 เซนติเมตร ที่มุมทั้งสี่วาดส่วนของวงกลม (เสี้ยววงกลม 1/4) รัศมี 7 เซนติเมตร โดยมีจุดศูนย์กลางที่มุมแต่ละมุม พื้นที่ส่วนของจัตุรัสที่ไม่อยู่ในเสี้ยววงกลมใด ๆ เป็นกี่ตารางเซนติเมตร (ใช้ π ≈ 22/7)","choices":["56","42","49","154"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Four quarter circles of radius 7 make one full circle: 22/7 × 7 × 7 = 154 cm². The square is 14 × 14 = 196 cm². Uncovered area = 196 − 154 = 42 cm².","th":"เสี้ยววงกลม 4 ชิ้นรัศมี 7 รวมกันเป็นวงกลม 1 วง พื้นที่ 22/7 × 7 × 7 = 154 ตร.ซม. จัตุรัสมีพื้นที่ 14 × 14 = 196 ตร.ซม. ส่วนที่เหลือ = 196 − 154 = 42 ตร.ซม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"โครงสร้างใดพบในเซลล์พืช แต่ไม่พบในเซลล์สัตว์","choices":["เยื่อหุ้มเซลล์","นิวเคลียส","ไมโทคอนเดรีย","ผนังเซลล์"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Plant cells have a cell wall (and chloroplasts) that animal cells lack. Both cell types have a cell membrane, a nucleus and mitochondria.","th":"เซลล์พืชมีผนังเซลล์ (และคลอโรพลาสต์) ซึ่งเซลล์สัตว์ไม่มี ส่วนเยื่อหุ้มเซลล์ นิวเคลียส และไมโทคอนเดรียพบได้ในเซลล์ทั้งสองชนิด"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"วงจรไฟฟ้ามีถ่านไฟฉาย 1 ชุด หลอดไฟ A ต่ออนุกรมกับหลอดไฟ B และ C ซึ่งต่อขนานกันอยู่ (หลอดทั้งสามเหมือนกันทุกประการ) ถ้าคลายหลอด B ออก ความสว่างของหลอด A และ C จะเปลี่ยนไปอย่างไร","choices":["A ไม่เปลี่ยน แต่ C สว่างขึ้น","A สว่างขึ้น และ C สว่างขึ้น","A หรี่ลง และ C หรี่ลง","A หรี่ลง แต่ C สว่างขึ้น"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Before: the circuit resistance is R + R/2 = 1.5R, so bulb A carries V/1.5R and C carries half of that, V/3R. After removing B: resistance = 2R, so A and C both carry V/2R. A's current falls (dimmer) and C's current rises (brighter).","th":"ก่อนคลาย: ความต้านทานรวม R + R/2 = 1.5R กระแสผ่าน A = V/1.5R และผ่าน C ครึ่งหนึ่ง = V/3R หลังคลาย B: ความต้านทานรวม 2R กระแสผ่าน A และ C = V/2R กระแสใน A ลดลงจึงหรี่ลง ส่วนกระแสใน C เพิ่มขึ้นจึงสว่างขึ้น"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":{"title":"ความสูงของต้นถั่วเขียวหลัง 2 สัปดาห์","rows":[["แสงต่อวัน (ชั่วโมง)","0","4","8","12"],["ความสูง (ซม.)","2","6","11","15"]]},"stem":"นักเรียนปลูกต้นถั่วเขียวในกระถาง 4 กระถาง ใช้ดิน น้ำ และพันธุ์เดียวกัน แต่ให้ได้รับแสงต่อวันต่างกัน แล้ววัดความสูงหลัง 2 สัปดาห์ ได้ผลดังตาราง ข้อสรุปใดเหมาะสมที่สุด","choices":["ในช่วงที่ทดลอง ยิ่งได้รับแสงต่อวันนานขึ้น ต้นถั่วเขียวยิ่งสูงมากขึ้น","ถ้าให้แสงวันละ 16 ชั่วโมง ต้นถั่วเขียวจะสูง 19 เซนติเมตรอย่างแน่นอน","ระยะเวลาที่ได้รับแสงเป็นตัวแปรควบคุมของการทดลองนี้","ปริมาณน้ำที่รดเป็นตัวแปรต้นของการทดลองนี้"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Light time is the independent variable (changed on purpose); water, soil and seed type are controlled. Height rises as light time rises from 0 to 12 hours, so that is the supported conclusion. Predicting an exact value at 16 hours goes beyond the data.","th":"ระยะเวลาที่ได้รับแสงเป็นตัวแปรต้น ส่วนน้ำ ดิน และพันธุ์เป็นตัวแปรควบคุม ข้อมูลแสดงว่าเมื่อแสงเพิ่มจาก 0 ถึง 12 ชั่วโมง ความสูงเพิ่มขึ้น จึงสรุปได้ว่ายิ่งได้แสงนานขึ้นยิ่งสูงมากขึ้นในช่วงที่ทดลอง การทำนายค่าแน่นอนที่ 16 ชั่วโมงเกินกว่าข้อมูลที่มี"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: My brother ___ to school by bus every day.","choices":["goes","go","gone","going"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"\"Every day\" shows a habit, so we use the present simple. With a singular subject (my brother) the verb takes -es: goes.","th":"\"every day\" บอกกิจวัตร จึงใช้ present simple ประธานเอกพจน์ (my brother) กริยาต้องเติม -es เป็น goes"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the best word: Dr. Suda is very ___. She checks every result three times before she writes her report.","choices":["careless","careful","lazy","noisy"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Checking every result three times shows she pays close attention, so \"careful\" fits. \"Careless\" means the opposite.","th":"การตรวจผลทุกครั้งถึงสามรอบแสดงว่าเธอละเอียดรอบคอบ จึงใช้ careful ส่วน careless มีความหมายตรงข้าม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"h","passage":"Mangroves grow where rivers meet the sea. Their tangled roots slow down the waves, so the soil behind them is not washed away. Small fish and crabs hide among the roots while they are young, and many of them later move out to the open sea. In the past, large areas of mangroves in Thailand were cut down to make shrimp farms. Today, some villages plant young mangrove trees every year, because they have learned that fewer mangroves mean fewer fish to catch.","table":null,"stem":"What can we infer about many of the fish that the villagers catch in the sea?","choices":["They eat the leaves of mangrove trees.","They can only live where rivers meet the sea.","They spent their early life among mangrove roots.","They are raised in shrimp farms."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text says young fish hide among the roots and later move to the open sea, and that fewer mangroves mean fewer fish to catch. So many fish caught at sea grew up among the mangrove roots.","th":"บทความบอกว่าปลาตัวเล็กหลบซ่อนอยู่ตามรากโกงกาง แล้วจึงออกไปสู่ทะเลเปิด และป่าชายเลนที่ลดลงทำให้จับปลาได้น้อยลง จึงอนุมานได้ว่าปลาที่จับได้ในทะเลจำนวนมากเคยเติบโตอยู่ตามรากโกงกาง"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำราชาศัพท์ที่ใช้แทนคำว่า \"กิน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์คือคำใด","choices":["เสวย","ประทับ","ทรงพระดำเนิน","บรรทม"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"For the king, \"to eat\" is เสวย. บรรทม means to sleep, ประทับ means to sit or stay, and ทรงพระดำเนิน means to walk.","th":"คำว่า \"กิน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์ใช้ว่า เสวย ส่วนบรรทม แปลว่า นอน ประทับ แปลว่า นั่งหรืออยู่ และทรงพระดำเนิน แปลว่า เดิน"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"สำนวน \"น้ำขึ้นให้รีบตัก\" มีความหมายตรงกับข้อใด","choices":["อย่าทำสิ่งใดรีบร้อนจนเกินไป","เมื่อมีโอกาสดีควรรีบทำ ไม่ปล่อยให้ผ่านไป","ควรช่วยเหลือผู้อื่นเมื่อเขาเดือดร้อน","ควรประหยัดน้ำไว้ใช้ในยามจำเป็น"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The saying means \"when the water rises, scoop it quickly\": when a good chance comes, take it at once before it passes.","th":"สำนวนนี้หมายถึง เมื่อมีโอกาสดีเข้ามา ควรรีบฉวยโอกาสนั้นไว้ก่อนที่จะผ่านพ้นไป"}}]}},{"exam":"gate","set":2,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 GATE Program — Practice set 2","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 GATE Program — ชุดฝึก 2"},"note":{"en":"40 questions: Mathematics 15, Science 15, English 5, Thai 5. DeepDistrict practice format based on the school's published subjects — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ: คณิตศาสตร์ 15 วิทยาศาสตร์ 15 ภาษาอังกฤษ 5 ภาษาไทย 5 — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ตามวิชาที่โรงเรียนประกาศ ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"จำนวน 5□72 หารด้วย 9 ลงตัว เลขโดดใน □ คือเลขใด","choices":["6","3","0","4"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"A number is divisible by 9 when its digit sum is. 5 + 7 + 2 = 14, and the next multiple of 9 is 18, so the missing digit is 18 − 14 = 4 (5,472 = 9 × 608).","th":"จำนวนที่หารด้วย 9 ลงตัวต้องมีผลบวกของเลขโดดหารด้วย 9 ลงตัว 5 + 7 + 2 = 14 พหุคูณของ 9 ถัดไปคือ 18 จึงต้องเติม 18 − 14 = 4 (5,472 = 9 × 608)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"รถไฟขบวนหนึ่งยาว 200 เมตร แล่นผ่านสะพานยาว 400 เมตร ตั้งแต่หัวรถเริ่มขึ้นสะพานจนท้ายรถพ้นสะพาน ใช้เวลา 30 วินาที รถไฟแล่นด้วยอัตราเร็วกี่กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง","choices":["24","20","48","72"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"To clear the bridge the train travels its own length plus the bridge: 200 + 400 = 600 m in 30 s = 20 m/s. 20 m/s × 3.6 = 72 km/h. (Using only 400 m gives 48 km/h.)","th":"รถไฟต้องเคลื่อนที่ได้ระยะเท่ากับความยาวขบวนบวกความยาวสะพาน 200 + 400 = 600 เมตร ใน 30 วินาที = 20 เมตร/วินาที × 3.6 = 72 กิโลเมตร/ชั่วโมง (ถ้าใช้แค่ 400 เมตร จะได้ 48 ซึ่งผิด)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ABCD เป็นรูปสี่เหลี่ยมผืนผ้า AB = 12 ซม. และ BC = 8 ซม. จุด E เป็นจุดกึ่งกลางของ BC และจุด F เป็นจุดกึ่งกลางของ CD พื้นที่ของรูปสามเหลี่ยม AEF เป็นกี่ตารางเซนติเมตร","choices":["40","48","32","36"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Subtract the three corner triangles from the rectangle (96 cm²): ABE = 12 × 4 ÷ 2 = 24, ECF = 4 × 6 ÷ 2 = 12, ADF = 8 × 6 ÷ 2 = 24. Area AEF = 96 − 24 − 12 − 24 = 36 cm².","th":"นำพื้นที่สี่เหลี่ยมผืนผ้า 96 ตร.ซม. ลบสามเหลี่ยมที่มุมทั้งสาม: ABE = 12 × 4 ÷ 2 = 24, ECF = 4 × 6 ÷ 2 = 12, ADF = 8 × 6 ÷ 2 = 24 พื้นที่ AEF = 96 − 24 − 12 − 24 = 36 ตร.ซม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"แก๊สใดที่พืชปล่อยออกมาจากกระบวนการสังเคราะห์ด้วยแสง","choices":["แก๊สไนโตรเจน","แก๊สออกซิเจน","ไอน้ำเท่านั้น","แก๊สคาร์บอนไดออกไซด์"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"In photosynthesis plants use carbon dioxide, water and light energy to make sugar and release oxygen gas.","th":"การสังเคราะห์ด้วยแสง พืชใช้แก๊สคาร์บอนไดออกไซด์ น้ำ และพลังงานแสง สร้างน้ำตาล และปล่อยแก๊สออกซิเจนออกมา"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"การเปลี่ยนแปลงใดเป็นการเปลี่ยนแปลงทางเคมี","choices":["ฉีกกระดาษเป็นชิ้นเล็ก ๆ","น้ำแข็งละลายเป็นน้ำ","ละลายน้ำตาลในน้ำ","ตะปูเหล็กเกิดสนิม"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Rust is a new substance (iron oxide) formed when iron reacts with oxygen and water, so it is a chemical change. Melting, dissolving and tearing change only form or state; no new substance forms.","th":"สนิมเหล็กเป็นสารใหม่ที่เกิดจากเหล็กทำปฏิกิริยากับออกซิเจนและน้ำ จึงเป็นการเปลี่ยนแปลงทางเคมี ส่วนการละลายของน้ำแข็ง การละลายน้ำตาล และการฉีกกระดาษ ไม่เกิดสารใหม่ จึงเป็นการเปลี่ยนแปลงทางกายภาพ"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":{"title":"ผลการทดลองแกว่งลูกตุ้ม","rows":[["การทดลอง","ความยาวเชือก (ซม.)","มวลลูกตุ้ม (g)","คาบ (วินาที)"],["1","25","50","1.0"],["2","25","100","1.0"],["3","100","50","2.0"],["4","100","100","2.0"]]},"stem":"นักเรียนทดลองแกว่งลูกตุ้มแล้วจับเวลาที่ใช้แกว่งครบ 1 รอบ (คาบ) ได้ผลดังตาราง ข้อสรุปใดถูกต้อง","choices":["คาบขึ้นกับมวลของลูกตุ้ม แต่ไม่ขึ้นกับความยาวเชือก","คาบขึ้นกับความยาวเชือก แต่ไม่ขึ้นกับมวลของลูกตุ้ม","เมื่อความยาวเชือกเพิ่มขึ้น 4 เท่า คาบจะเพิ่มขึ้น 4 เท่า","ทั้งมวลและความยาวเชือกมีผลต่อคาบเท่า ๆ กัน"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Trials 1 and 2 (same length, different mass) give the same period, so mass has no effect. Trials 1 and 3 (same mass, length × 4) change the period from 1.0 s to 2.0 s, so length matters — and the period only doubles, not ×4.","th":"การทดลองที่ 1 และ 2 ความยาวเท่ากัน มวลต่างกัน ได้คาบเท่ากัน แสดงว่ามวลไม่มีผล การทดลองที่ 1 และ 3 มวลเท่ากัน ความยาวเพิ่ม 4 เท่า คาบเปลี่ยนจาก 1.0 เป็น 2.0 วินาที แสดงว่าความยาวมีผล และคาบเพิ่มเพียง 2 เท่า ไม่ใช่ 4 เท่า"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: There ___ some milk in the fridge.","choices":["is","are","be","have"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Milk is an uncountable noun, so it takes a singular verb: there is some milk.","th":"milk เป็นคำนามนับไม่ได้ จึงใช้กริยาเอกพจน์ there is some milk"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which word is the opposite of \"ancient\"?","choices":["famous","huge","modern","old"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"\"Ancient\" means very old, from long ago. Its opposite is \"modern\" (new, of the present time). \"Old\" has a similar meaning.","th":"ancient แปลว่า เก่าแก่โบราณ คำตรงข้ามคือ modern (ทันสมัย ปัจจุบัน) ส่วน old มีความหมายใกล้เคียงกัน ไม่ใช่ตรงข้าม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"h","passage":"Nida wanted to know which kind of bag kept ice frozen the longest. She put the same amount of ice into a paper bag, a plastic bag and a cloth bag, and left them all in the sun. She checked every ten minutes. The ice in the plastic bag melted first, while the ice in the cloth bag lasted the longest. Nida was surprised, because she had expected the plastic bag to win. She decided to repeat the test the next day to make sure her result was not a mistake.","table":null,"stem":"Why did Nida decide to repeat the test the next day?","choices":["Because the ice in the cloth bag never melted.","To check that her result was reliable.","Because she wanted to use more ice.","Because her teacher said the result was wrong."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Nida was surprised by the result and repeated the test \"to make sure her result was not a mistake\" — that is, to check it was reliable. The other reasons are not in the text.","th":"นิดาประหลาดใจกับผลการทดลอง จึงทำซ้ำ \"to make sure her result was not a mistake\" คือเพื่อตรวจสอบว่าผลเชื่อถือได้ เหตุผลอื่นไม่ได้กล่าวไว้ในเรื่อง"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำราชาศัพท์ที่ใช้แทนคำว่า \"นอน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์คือคำใด","choices":["ตรัส","บรรทม","สรง","เสวย"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"For the king, \"to sleep\" is บรรทม. เสวย means to eat, สรง means to bathe, and ตรัส means to speak.","th":"คำว่า \"นอน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์ใช้ว่า บรรทม ส่วนเสวย แปลว่า กิน สรง แปลว่า อาบน้ำ และตรัส แปลว่า พูด"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"สำนวน \"ช้า ๆ ได้พร้าเล่มงาม\" มีความหมายตรงกับข้อใด","choices":["คนขี้เกียจมักได้สิ่งที่ไม่ดี","ควรรีบทำงานให้เสร็จก่อนผู้อื่น","ทำงานอย่างประณีตรอบคอบ แม้จะช้าแต่ได้ผลดี","ของดีมักมีราคาแพง"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The saying (\"slowly, you get a fine machete\") means careful, unhurried work gives a good result.","th":"สำนวนนี้หมายถึง การทำสิ่งใดอย่างค่อยเป็นค่อยไป ประณีตรอบคอบ แม้จะใช้เวลานาน แต่ผลงานที่ได้จะดี"}}]}},{"exam":"gate","set":3,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 GATE Program — Practice set 3","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 GATE Program — ชุดฝึก 3"},"note":{"en":"40 questions: Mathematics 15, Science 15, English 5, Thai 5. DeepDistrict practice format based on the school's published subjects — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ: คณิตศาสตร์ 15 วิทยาศาสตร์ 15 ภาษาอังกฤษ 5 ภาษาไทย 5 — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ตามวิชาที่โรงเรียนประกาศ ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"48 ÷ 4 × 3 − 2² × 5 มีค่าเท่าใด","choices":["4","160","16","26"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Powers first: 2² = 4. Then × and ÷ from left to right: 48 ÷ 4 × 3 = 36 and 4 × 5 = 20. Finally 36 − 20 = 16. (Doing 4 × 3 first gives 48 ÷ 12 and leads to a wrong answer.)","th":"คิดเลขยกกำลังก่อน 2² = 4 แล้วคูณหารจากซ้ายไปขวา 48 ÷ 4 × 3 = 36 และ 4 × 5 = 20 สุดท้าย 36 − 20 = 16 (ถ้าคูณ 4 × 3 ก่อนจะได้ 48 ÷ 12 ซึ่งผิดลำดับ)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ชายสองคนอยู่ห่างกัน 36 กิโลเมตร เดินเข้าหากันด้วยอัตราเร็ว 5 และ 7 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง สุนัขตัวหนึ่งวิ่งกลับไปกลับมาระหว่างชายทั้งสองด้วยอัตราเร็ว 15 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง ตั้งแต่เริ่มเดินจนทั้งสองพบกัน สุนัขวิ่งได้ระยะทางทั้งหมดกี่กิโลเมตร","choices":["45","30","36","54"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The men close the gap at 5 + 7 = 12 km/h, so they meet after 36 ÷ 12 = 3 hours. The dog runs for those same 3 hours: 15 × 3 = 45 km. No need to follow each back-and-forth trip.","th":"ทั้งสองเดินเข้าหากันด้วยอัตราเร็วรวม 5 + 7 = 12 กม./ชม. จึงพบกันหลัง 36 ÷ 12 = 3 ชั่วโมง สุนัขวิ่งตลอด 3 ชั่วโมงนั้น ระยะทาง = 15 × 3 = 45 กม. ไม่ต้องคิดทีละเที่ยว"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ลูกบาศก์ไม้ยาวด้านละ 6 ซม. ทาสีแดงทุกด้าน แล้วตัดเป็นลูกบาศก์เล็กยาวด้านละ 1 ซม. ทั้งหมด จะมีลูกบาศก์เล็กที่ถูกทาสีแดงเพียง 2 ด้านกี่ลูก","choices":["48","96","8","64"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Cubes with exactly two red faces lie along the 12 edges but not at the corners: each edge has 6 − 2 = 4 such cubes, so 12 × 4 = 48. (96 have one red face, 64 have none, 8 corners have three.)","th":"ลูกบาศก์เล็กที่มีสีสองด้านอยู่ตามขอบ 12 เส้น ยกเว้นที่มุม ขอบละ 6 − 2 = 4 ลูก รวม 12 × 4 = 48 ลูก (สีด้านเดียวมี 96 ลูก ไม่มีสีเลย 64 ลูก และที่มุมมีสีสามด้าน 8 ลูก)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ส่วนใดของเซลล์ทำหน้าที่ควบคุมการทำงานของเซลล์และเก็บสารพันธุกรรม","choices":["แวคิวโอล","นิวเคลียส","เยื่อหุ้มเซลล์","ไซโทพลาซึม"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The nucleus contains the genetic material (DNA) and controls the cell's activities. The cell membrane controls what enters and leaves; the cytoplasm and vacuole do not control the cell.","th":"นิวเคลียสเก็บสารพันธุกรรม (DNA) และควบคุมการทำงานของเซลล์ เยื่อหุ้มเซลล์ควบคุมการเข้าออกของสาร ส่วนไซโทพลาซึมและแวคิวโอลไม่ได้ทำหน้าที่ควบคุมเซลล์"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ตะโกนหน้าหน้าผาแล้วได้ยินเสียงสะท้อนกลับมาหลังจากตะโกน 4 วินาที ถ้าอัตราเร็วเสียงในอากาศเท่ากับ 340 เมตรต่อวินาที หน้าผาอยู่ห่างออกไปกี่เมตร","choices":["1360","340","680","85"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"In 4 s the sound goes to the cliff and back: 340 × 4 = 1,360 m in total. The cliff is half of that, 680 m away.","th":"ใน 4 วินาที เสียงเดินทางไปถึงหน้าผาแล้วสะท้อนกลับ รวม 340 × 4 = 1,360 เมตร หน้าผาจึงอยู่ห่างครึ่งหนึ่ง คือ 680 เมตร"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":{"title":"ความหนาแน่นของของเหลว","rows":[["ของเหลว","ความหนาแน่น (g/cm³)"],["น้ำมันพืช","0.92"],["น้ำ","1.00"],["น้ำเชื่อมเข้มข้น","1.40"],["สารละลาย X","1.80"]]},"stem":"ก้อนวัสดุรูปสี่เหลี่ยมมุมฉากขนาด 4 × 5 × 10 ซม. มีมวล 300 กรัม เมื่อนำไปใส่ในของเหลวแต่ละชนิดในตาราง ก้อนวัสดุนี้จะลอยในของเหลวใด","choices":["สารละลาย X","น้ำเชื่อมเข้มข้น","น้ำมันพืช","น้ำ"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Volume = 4 × 5 × 10 = 200 cm³, so density = 300 ÷ 200 = 1.5 g/cm³. It floats only in a liquid denser than 1.5 g/cm³: liquid X (1.80). It sinks in oil, water and syrup (1.40).","th":"ปริมาตร = 4 × 5 × 10 = 200 ลบ.ซม. ความหนาแน่น = 300 ÷ 200 = 1.5 g/cm³ จะลอยได้เฉพาะในของเหลวที่หนาแน่นกว่า 1.5 คือสารละลาย X (1.80) ส่วนน้ำมันพืช น้ำ และน้ำเชื่อมเข้มข้น (1.40) หนาแน่นน้อยกว่า วัสดุจึงจม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: Our school sports day is ___ Friday.","choices":["by","at","on","in"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"We use \"on\" with days and dates: on Friday, on 5 May. \"In\" is for months and years, \"at\" for clock times.","th":"ใช้ on กับวันและวันที่ เช่น on Friday ส่วน in ใช้กับเดือนและปี และ at ใช้กับเวลา"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the word closest in meaning to \"enormous\" in this sentence: The elephant was enormous.","choices":["tiny","huge","friendly","noisy"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"\"Enormous\" means extremely big, the same as \"huge\". \"Tiny\" is the opposite.","th":"enormous แปลว่า ใหญ่มาก มีความหมายเดียวกับ huge ส่วน tiny มีความหมายตรงข้าม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"h","passage":"Dear parents,\nThe school trip to the Science Museum will now take place on Friday 14 November instead of Thursday 13 November, because the museum is closed for repairs on Thursday. Buses will leave at 7.30 a.m., half an hour earlier than planned, so that students can join the planetarium show at 9.00. Students should bring a packed lunch, as the museum café will not be open. Please return the signed form by Monday 10 November.","table":null,"stem":"According to the notice, what time were the buses first planned to leave?","choices":["7.30 a.m.","8.30 a.m.","8.00 a.m.","9.00 a.m."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The buses will now leave at 7.30 a.m., \"half an hour earlier than planned\". So the original plan was half an hour later: 8.00 a.m. 9.00 is the planetarium show.","th":"ประกาศบอกว่ารถออก 7.30 น. ซึ่ง \"เร็วกว่าที่วางแผนไว้ครึ่งชั่วโมง\" เวลาเดิมจึงช้ากว่าครึ่งชั่วโมง คือ 8.00 น. ส่วน 9.00 น. เป็นเวลาการแสดงท้องฟ้าจำลอง"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำราชาศัพท์ที่ใช้แทนคำว่า \"ป่วย\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์คือคำใด","choices":["บรรทม","ประชวร","เสด็จ","ประทับ"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"For the king, \"to be ill\" is ประชวร. ประทับ means to sit or stay, เสด็จ means to go, and บรรทม means to sleep.","th":"คำว่า \"ป่วย\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์ใช้ว่า ประชวร ส่วนประทับ แปลว่า นั่งหรืออยู่ เสด็จ แปลว่า ไป และบรรทม แปลว่า นอน"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"สำนวน \"ตีตนไปก่อนไข้\" มีความหมายตรงกับข้อใด","choices":["ทำร้ายตัวเองเพื่อหนีปัญหา","ลงโทษตนเองเมื่อทำผิด","ป้องกันโรคไว้ก่อนจะเจ็บป่วย","วิตกกังวลกับเรื่องที่ยังไม่เกิดขึ้น"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The idiom means worrying or suffering over something that has not happened yet. It is not about preventing illness.","th":"สำนวนนี้หมายถึง การวิตกกังวลหรือทุกข์ร้อนไปก่อนกับเรื่องที่ยังไม่เกิดขึ้น ไม่ได้หมายถึงการป้องกันโรค"}}]}},{"exam":"ep","set":1,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 English Program (EPLUS+) — Practice set 1","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 English Program (EPLUS+) — ชุดฝึก 1"},"note":{"en":"40 questions in English: English 20, Mathematics 10, Science 10. The real admission also has an English interview. DeepDistrict practice format — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ เป็นภาษาอังกฤษ: ภาษาอังกฤษ 20 คณิตศาสตร์ 10 วิทยาศาสตร์ 10 (การสอบจริงมีสัมภาษณ์ภาษาอังกฤษด้วย) — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: \"My sister ___ to school by bus every day.\"","choices":["is go","goes","going","go"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"\"Every day\" shows a habit, so we use the present simple. With he/she/it the verb takes -s/-es: \"goes\".","th":"\"every day\" บอกกิจวัตร จึงใช้ present simple และประธานเอกพจน์บุรุษที่ 3 (my sister) ต้องเติม -es เป็น \"goes\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct words: \"This bridge ___ in 1932.\"","choices":["built","was built","is building","was build"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"A bridge cannot build itself, so we need the passive. It happened in the past: was + past participle = \"was built\".","th":"สะพานสร้างตัวเองไม่ได้ จึงใช้ passive และเป็นอดีต (1932): was + V3 = \"was built\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"Last year, the students of Class 6/2 turned an empty corner of their school field into a vegetable garden. At first, the soil was hard and full of stones, so they mixed in compost made from fallen leaves and fruit peel from the canteen. Each group looked after one bed and kept a notebook about watering and growth. The morning glory grew fastest and was ready to pick in less than a month, while the pumpkins took almost four months. In the rainy season, some seedlings were washed away, so the class learned to build low bamboo walls around the beds. Today the canteen buys the vegetables at a fair price, and the money pays for new seeds. Their teacher says the garden has taught the children more than any textbook: patience, teamwork and how food really reaches their plates.","table":null,"stem":"Why did the students add compost to the soil?","choices":["It was the rainy season.","The soil was hard and full of stones.","The seeds were too old.","The canteen asked them to."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The text says the soil was hard and full of stones, \"so\" they mixed in compost.","th":"เรื่องบอกว่าดินแข็งและมีหินมาก \"so\" จึงผสมปุ๋ยหมัก"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"What is 3/4 + 1/6?","choices":["1 1/12","4/10","10/12","11/12"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Use the common denominator 12: 3/4 = 9/12 and 1/6 = 2/12, so 9/12 + 2/12 = 11/12.","th":"ทำส่วนให้เท่ากันเป็น 12: 3/4 = 9/12, 1/6 = 2/12 รวมได้ 11/12"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"A rectangle is 12 cm long and its perimeter is 40 cm. What is its area?","choices":["64 cm²","120 cm²","96 cm²","80 cm²"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Length + width = 40 ÷ 2 = 20, so the width is 8 cm. Area = 12 × 8 = 96 cm².","th":"ยาว + กว้าง = 40 ÷ 2 = 20 กว้าง = 8 ซม. พื้นที่ = 12 × 8 = 96 ตร.ซม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"What is the next number in the pattern 2, 5, 10, 17, 26, …?","choices":["35","37","36","39"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The differences are 3, 5, 7, 9, so the next difference is 11: 26 + 11 = 37. (Each term is n × n + 1.)","th":"ผลต่างเป็น 3, 5, 7, 9 ตัวถัดไปเพิ่ม 11 ได้ 26 + 11 = 37"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which part of a plant takes in water from the soil?","choices":["The roots","The leaves","The fruit","The flowers"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Roots grow into the soil and absorb water and minerals; the stem then carries the water up to the leaves.","th":"รากชอนไชในดินและดูดน้ำกับแร่ธาตุ แล้วลำต้นลำเลียงน้ำขึ้นไปยังใบ"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"In the food chain grass → grasshopper → frog → snake, which organism is the primary consumer?","choices":["Snake","Frog","Grasshopper","Grass"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The primary consumer is the first animal that eats the producer. Grass is the producer, and the grasshopper eats it.","th":"ผู้บริโภคลำดับที่ 1 คือสัตว์ที่กินผู้ผลิต หญ้าเป็นผู้ผลิต ตั๊กแตนกินหญ้า"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Nida wants to find out whether the amount of sunlight affects how tall bean plants grow. Which variable must she keep the same for every plant?","choices":["The amount of sunlight each plant gets","Nothing; every variable may change","The final height of each plant","The amount of water each plant gets"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Sunlight is the variable she changes and height is what she measures. To make it a fair test, other things such as water must stay the same.","th":"แสงแดดคือตัวแปรต้น ความสูงคือตัวแปรตาม ปริมาณน้ำต้องควบคุมให้เท่ากันจึงเป็นการทดลองที่ยุติธรรม"}}]}},{"exam":"ep","set":2,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 English Program (EPLUS+) — Practice set 2","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 English Program (EPLUS+) — ชุดฝึก 2"},"note":{"en":"40 questions in English: English 20, Mathematics 10, Science 10. The real admission also has an English interview. DeepDistrict practice format — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ เป็นภาษาอังกฤษ: ภาษาอังกฤษ 20 คณิตศาสตร์ 10 วิทยาศาสตร์ 10 (การสอบจริงมีสัมภาษณ์ภาษาอังกฤษด้วย) — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct words: \"Look! The children ___ in the garden.\"","choices":["plays","play","played","are playing"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"\"Look!\" tells us the action is happening now, so we use the present continuous: \"are playing\".","th":"\"Look!\" แสดงว่ากำลังเกิดขึ้นขณะนี้ จึงใช้ present continuous \"are playing\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct words: \"English ___ in many countries around the world.\"","choices":["is speaking","spoke","speaks","is spoken"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"A language does not speak; people speak it. So we use the present simple passive: \"is spoken\".","th":"ภาษาพูดเองไม่ได้ คนเป็นผู้พูด จึงใช้ passive ปัจจุบัน \"is spoken\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"Every year, female green turtles swim thousands of kilometres to lay their eggs on the same beaches where they were born. On some islands in the Gulf of Thailand, volunteers walk along the sand at night to look for new nests. Because a turtle may lay more than a hundred eggs at a time, every nest is precious. The volunteers carefully move the eggs to a protected hatchery, where they are safe from dogs, crabs and people who might sell them. After about two months, the baby turtles break out of their shells and are released into the sea at night. Even so, scientists believe that only about one in a thousand will survive to become an adult. Plastic bags, which look like jellyfish in the water, are one of the biggest dangers, because turtles often eat them by mistake.","table":null,"stem":"Why do the volunteers move the eggs to a hatchery?","choices":["Because the turtles cannot find the beach","To keep them safe from animals and people","To make them hatch faster","To sell them to tourists"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The hatchery keeps the eggs \"safe from dogs, crabs and people who might sell them\".","th":"โรงเพาะฟักช่วยให้ไข่ \"ปลอดภัยจากสุนัข ปู และคนที่อาจนำไปขาย\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"What is 2.5 × 0.4?","choices":["2.9","0.1","10","1"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"2.5 × 0.4 = 25 × 4 ÷ 100 = 100 ÷ 100 = 1.","th":"2.5 × 0.4 = 25 × 4 ÷ 100 = 1"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 48° and 67°. What is the third angle?","choices":["115°","65°","55°","75°"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The angles of a triangle add up to 180°: 180 − 48 − 67 = 65°.","th":"มุมภายในสามเหลี่ยมรวม 180° ดังนั้น 180 − 48 − 67 = 65°"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"What is the value of 3x + 2y when x = 4 and y = 5?","choices":["26","20","22","17"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"3 × 4 + 2 × 5 = 12 + 10 = 22.","th":"3 × 4 + 2 × 5 = 12 + 10 = 22"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which gas do plants take in from the air for photosynthesis?","choices":["Carbon dioxide","Oxygen","Nitrogen","Hydrogen"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Plants use carbon dioxide and water, with light energy, to make sugar; oxygen is given out.","th":"พืชใช้คาร์บอนไดออกไซด์และน้ำ ร่วมกับพลังงานแสง สร้างน้ำตาล และปล่อยออกซิเจนออกมา"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which of these animals is a mammal?","choices":["Shark","Whale","Penguin","Frog"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Whales breathe air with lungs, are warm-blooded and feed their young on milk, so they are mammals. A shark is a fish, a penguin a bird, a frog an amphibian.","th":"วาฬหายใจด้วยปอดและเลี้ยงลูกด้วยนม จึงเป็นสัตว์เลี้ยงลูกด้วยนม ฉลามเป็นปลา เพนกวินเป็นนก กบเป็นสัตว์สะเทินน้ำสะเทินบก"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"A box is pushed to the right with a force of 50 N. Friction acts on it with a force of 20 N to the left. What is the net (overall) force on the box?","choices":["70 N to the right","0 N","30 N to the right","30 N to the left"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The forces act in opposite directions, so subtract: 50 − 20 = 30 N, in the direction of the bigger force (right).","th":"แรงมีทิศตรงข้ามกันจึงนำมาลบกัน 50 − 20 = 30 N ทิศตามแรงที่มากกว่า คือไปทางขวา"}}]}},{"exam":"ep","set":3,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 English Program (EPLUS+) — Practice set 3","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 English Program (EPLUS+) — ชุดฝึก 3"},"note":{"en":"40 questions in English: English 20, Mathematics 10, Science 10. The real admission also has an English interview. DeepDistrict practice format — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ เป็นภาษาอังกฤษ: ภาษาอังกฤษ 20 คณิตศาสตร์ 10 วิทยาศาสตร์ 10 (การสอบจริงมีสัมภาษณ์ภาษาอังกฤษด้วย) — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: \"We ___ football every Saturday morning.\"","choices":["playing","plays","play","are play"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"\"Every Saturday\" is a habit, so we use the present simple. With \"we\" the verb has no -s: \"play\".","th":"\"every Saturday\" เป็นกิจวัตร ใช้ present simple ประธาน we ไม่เติม -s จึงเป็น \"play\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct words: \"The winners ___ their prizes by the principal next Monday.\"","choices":["gave","will be given","are giving","will give"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The principal gives the prizes, so the winners receive the action: passive. \"Next Monday\" is the future: \"will be given\".","th":"ผู้ชนะเป็นผู้ได้รับรางวัล (ถูกกระทำ) จึงใช้ passive และเป็นอนาคต (next Monday) \"will be given\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"On a hot afternoon, the centre of Bangkok can be several degrees warmer than the farmland outside the city. Scientists call this the \"urban heat island\" effect. Roads, roofs and concrete walls absorb sunlight during the day and slowly release the heat at night, so the city does not cool down as quickly as the countryside. Air conditioners make the problem worse, because they push hot air out of buildings into the streets. Trees, on the other hand, help in two ways: their leaves give shade, and the water they release through their leaves cools the air around them. Some cities have started painting roofs white, since light colours reflect more sunlight than dark ones. Others are building \"green roofs\" covered with plants. None of these ideas will solve the problem alone, but together they could make city life far more comfortable.","table":null,"stem":"According to the passage, which place is usually cooler on a hot afternoon?","choices":["Streets near air conditioners","Rooms with concrete walls","The centre of Bangkok","The farmland outside the city"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The first sentence says the centre of Bangkok can be several degrees warmer than the farmland outside the city, so the farmland is cooler.","th":"ประโยคแรกบอกว่าใจกลางกรุงเทพฯ ร้อนกว่าพื้นที่เกษตรนอกเมือง พื้นที่เกษตรนอกเมืองจึงเย็นกว่า"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"What is 0.75 written as a fraction in its simplest form?","choices":["75/10","7/5","3/4","3/5"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"0.75 = 75/100. Divide top and bottom by 25: 3/4.","th":"0.75 = 75/100 หารด้วย 25 ทั้งเศษและส่วน ได้ 3/4"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Three angles on a straight line are in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4. What is the size of the largest angle?","choices":["60°","40°","80°","160°"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Angles on a straight line add up to 180°. 2 + 3 + 4 = 9 parts, so 1 part = 20°. Largest = 4 × 20 = 80°.","th":"มุมบนเส้นตรงรวม 180° รวม 9 ส่วน ส่วนละ 20° มุมใหญ่สุด 4 × 20 = 80°"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"After a 20% discount, a bag costs 1,440 baht. What was the original price?","choices":["1,800 baht","1,152 baht","1,200 baht","1,728 baht"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"After a 20% discount you pay 80% of the price. 80% = 1,440, so 100% = 1,440 ÷ 0.8 = 1,800 baht. (Adding 20% of 1,440 gives the wrong 1,728.)","th":"ลด 20% ต้องจ่าย 80% ของราคาเดิม 80% = 1,440 บาท ราคาเดิม = 1,440 ÷ 0.8 = 1,800 บาท"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which of these is true of ALL living things?","choices":["They have bones.","They make their own food.","They grow and reproduce.","They can move from place to place."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Every living thing grows and reproduces. Plants cannot walk about, animals do not make their own food, and many living things have no bones.","th":"สิ่งมีชีวิตทุกชนิดเจริญเติบโตและสืบพันธุ์ได้ พืชเคลื่อนที่ไปมาไม่ได้ สัตว์สร้างอาหารเองไม่ได้ และหลายชนิดไม่มีกระดูก"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which of these is a mixture?","choices":["Pure water","Gold","Sea water","Oxygen gas"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Sea water is water with salts and other substances mixed in, so it is a mixture. Pure water, oxygen and gold are pure substances.","th":"น้ำทะเลมีน้ำ เกลือ และสารอื่นผสมกัน จึงเป็นสารผสม ส่วนน้ำบริสุทธิ์ ออกซิเจน และทองคำเป็นสารบริสุทธิ์"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"ep","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"A ball is thrown straight up. Which statement is true at its highest point?","choices":["Gravity stops acting on it.","Its kinetic energy is at its greatest.","Its speed is zero for a moment, and gravity is still pulling it down.","Its potential energy is at its lowest."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"At the top the ball stops for an instant (kinetic energy is lowest, potential energy highest), but gravity never switches off, so it falls back.","th":"ที่จุดสูงสุดลูกบอลหยุดชั่วขณะ (พลังงานจลน์ต่ำสุด พลังงานศักย์สูงสุด) แต่แรงโน้มถ่วงยังกระทำอยู่ จึงตกลงมา"}}]}}];
